draw(Circle((5.3,3.8), .5));
[/asy]

On a 6 by 6 grid of points, what fraction of the larger square's area is inside the new shaded square? Place the bottom-left vertex of the square at grid point (3,3) and the square rotates 45 degrees (square's sides are diagonals of the smaller grid cells).
```
[asy]
size(6cm);
fill((3,3)--(4,4)--(5,3)--(4,2)--cycle,gray(0.7));
dot((1,1));
for (int i = 0; i <= 6; ++i) {
    draw((0,i)--(6,i));
    draw((i,0)--(i,6));
    for (int j = 0; j <= 6; ++j) {
        dot((i,j));
    }
}
draw((3,3)--(4,4)--(5,3)--(4,2)--cycle);
[/asy]
```

A square $EFGH$ is inscribed in the region bound by the parabola $y = x^2 - 8x + 16$ and the $x$-axis. Find the area of square $EFGH$.

[asy]
unitsize(0.8 cm);

real parab2 (real x) {
  return(x^2 - 8*x + 16);
}

pair E, F, G, H;
real x = -2 + 2*sqrt(3);

E = (4 - x,0);
F = (4 + x,0);
G = (4 + x,-2*x);
H = (4 - x,-2*x);

draw(graph(parab2,0.5,7.5));
draw(E--H--G--F);
draw((0,0)--(8,0));

label("$E$", E, N);
label("$F$", F, N);
label("$G$", G, SE);
label("$H$", H, SW);
[/asy]
